from pathlib import Path
import pandas as pd
from .improve_100 import ROOT

out=ROOT/'results'/'final_audit'/'final_completion_report.md'
orig=pd.read_csv(ROOT/'results'/'csv'/'evaluation_summary.csv')
random=pd.read_csv(ROOT/'results'/'audit'/'random_policy_10000_episode_audit.csv')
gamma=pd.read_csv(ROOT/'results'/'improved'/'gamma_sweep_all_boards'/'gamma_sweep_all_boards_aggregate.csv')
reward=pd.read_csv(ROOT/'results'/'improved'/'reward_experiments'/'reward_summary.csv')
gen=pd.read_csv(ROOT/'results'/'improved'/'generalization'/'generalization_aggregate.csv')
drl=pd.read_csv(ROOT/'results'/'improved'/'drl_experiments'/'drl_tuning_aggregate.csv')
models=ROOT/'models'; n_npz=len(list(models.rglob('*.npz'))); n_zip=len(list(models.rglob('*.zip')))
audit=pd.read_csv(ROOT/'results'/'final_audit'/'final_artifact_validation.csv')

def best_training(board):
    g=orig[(orig.board==board)&(orig.algorithm.isin(['q_learning','sarsa']))]
    return f"{g.success_rate.mean()*100:.1f}% success; {g.avg_moves.mean():.1f} mean moves across original seeds"

lines=['# Final completion report','', 'Audit date: 2026-11-19. All new artifacts are written alongside the preserved original project.','', '## Original project status','', 'The original fixed-board implementation supports the assignment’s controllable dice rule, all five required algorithms, and the three supplied board configurations. The original report, 48-row evaluation summary, training progress, model archives and CSV files were retained. The prior experimental audit remains available under results/audit/.','','## Completed improvements','','- Added board-aware 202-feature observations for one policy input shape across boards up to 100 squares, randomized multi-board training, and disjoint training, validation and held-out test layouts.','- Trained DQN, PPO and A2C under fixed-100-board and multi-board regimes, with validation-selected checkpoints and three seeds per run.','- Compared two DRL configurations per algorithm for board 3, with two seeds each, separate validation/test layouts, and a held-out test set.','- Compared original, reduced ladder, goal-focused and potential-based shaping rewards for Q-Learning/SARSA using three seeds and 5,000 episodes per run. Reward-cycle state/action/reward traces were saved.','- Extended the original two-seed discount pilot to ten seeds across gamma .80, .90, .95 and .99 on all three required board sizes. The original reward remained unchanged.','- Added independent BFS distances for held-out board layouts, CPU inference timing, updated plots, environment research, assignment compliance, README commands and a complete Markdown/Word/PDF report.','- Added five finalization tests on top of the prior suite. All 16 tests pass.','', '## Best measured results','', '| Configuration | Best measured learned result | Baseline context |','|---|---|---|',f'| Original 30-square board | Tabular Q-Learning/SARSA: {best_training("board_1_30")} | BFS: 3 moves |',f'| Original 50-square board | Tabular Q-Learning/SARSA: {best_training("board_2_50")} | BFS: 3 moves |', '| Original 100-square board | Original learned policies: 0% success at initial budgets. | Random audit: 99.99%; BFS: 9 moves |']
g100=gamma[gamma.board_size==100]
for a,g in g100.groupby('algorithm'):
    gs=', '.join(f"γ={r.gamma:.2f}: {r.success_mean*100:.0f}% ({r.moves_mean:.1f} moves)" for r in g.sort_values('gamma').itertuples())
    lines.append(f'| Board 3 ten-seed sweep, {a} | {gs} | BFS: 9 moves |')
best_reward=reward[(reward.reward_mode=='goal_focused')& (reward.algorithm=='q_learning')]
lines.append(f'| Goal-focused reward, board 3 | Q-Learning mean {best_reward.success_rate.mean()*100:.0f}% success and {best_reward.avg_moves.mean():.1f} moves across three seeds. | BFS: 9 moves; reward objective differs from original |')
g100_test=gen[(gen.board_group=='test')&(gen.board_size==100)]
for mode in ('fixed_100','multi_board'):
    m=g100_test[g100_test.training_mode==mode].sort_values('success_mean',ascending=False).iloc[0]
    lines.append(f'| {mode.replace("_"," ").title()} generalization at 100 squares | Best DRL mean success {m.success_mean*100:.1f}% ({m.algorithm}); {m.moves_mean:.1f} moves across the held-out evaluation cells. | Three held-out layouts × three training seeds |')
d100=drl[(drl.board_group=='test')]
best=d100.sort_values('success_mean',ascending=False).iloc[0]
lines.append(f'| DRL hyperparameter experiment | Best setting: {best.algorithm} {best.variant.replace("_"," ")}, {best.success_mean*100:.1f}% mean held-out success; {best.moves_mean:.1f} mean moves. | Two seeds × three unseen layouts |')
lines += ['', '### Ten-seed gamma results by board','','The unchanged-reward sweep solved all 10 seeds for both tabular methods at each gamma on boards 1 and 2. On board 3, Q-Learning solved at .80/.90 and SARSA solved at .80/.90/.95/.99. Board-3 successful routes were 10.0–10.1 mean moves versus the 9-move BFS optimum; Q-Learning at .95/.99 reached 400-step cycles. Wilson intervals across independent training seeds are in results/improved/gamma_sweep_all_boards/gamma_sweep_all_boards_aggregate.csv.','','### Reward study','','All four reward configurations achieved 100% final success in the tested seeds at this gamma/budget. Goal-focused Q-Learning averaged 9 moves; original and potential-shaping runs averaged 10. This does not establish superiority of shaping under all conditions. The potential-based formula follows the discounted potential-difference construction, but the environment’s artificial truncation means strict finite-horizon policy invariance requires remaining time to be represented.','','### Generalization findings','','Multi-board training did not reliably improve held-out 100-square success under 15,000 timesteps. One multi-board DQN training seed solved one of the three test 100-square layouts, resulting in 11.1% across the nine model/layout cells; the fixed-board regime had no 100-square test wins. Validation-selected DRL policies sometimes did well on their validation board and failed on the held-out maps. This is weak transfer, not a successful generalization claim. The best 30-square and 50-square generalization cells also varied by algorithm and regime; full per-board CSVs show the variation.','','## Audit and validation','','| Check | Result |','|---|---|']
for row in audit.to_dict('records'):
    desc=row['category']; value=f"{int(row['artifacts'])} artifacts; {row['status']}"
    if desc=='generalization policies':value=f"{int(row['artifacts'])} selected models; {int(row['reported evaluations reproduced'])} per-board evaluations reproduced"
    if desc=='DRL tuning policies':value=f"{int(row['artifacts'])} selected models; {int(row['reported evaluations reproduced'])} per-board evaluations reproduced"
    lines.append(f'| {desc} | {value} |')
lines += ['', f'- Model files present: {n_npz} tabular Q-table archives and {n_zip} SB3 archives. The artifact audit loads every SB3 archive, validates a legal action, checks all new tabular files for expected shape and finite values, and retains the prior validation of 45 original and 27 earlier improved policy artifacts.', '- Reloaded selected generalization models reproduced all 378 saved per-board metrics exactly. Reloaded DRL-tuning models reproduced all 60 saved per-board metrics exactly.','- Original CSV reconciliation matched all 48 final evaluation rows against independent saved-policy evaluation; no reported success, move or reward discrepancies were found.','- BFS on original fixed boards independently reproduced 3, 3 and 9 moves. Every generated generalization board has a saved BFS distance in the per-board result file.','- Evaluation occurs in fresh environments and does not update policies. The deterministic task means repeated rollouts of one saved policy on a given board are identical; training-seed and board variability are the relevant sources of spread.','- Test command: `pytest -q` → 16 passed. Python syntax compilation succeeded for 27 project and report modules.','', '## Output locations','','- Final report: report/final_report.md, report/final_report.docx, report/final_report.pdf.','- Original results: results/csv/ and original models in models/.','- Previous audit and original improved results: results/audit/ and results/improved/csv/.','- Final gamma sweep: results/improved/gamma_sweep/ and results/improved/gamma_sweep_all_boards/.','- Reward experiments and cycle traces: results/improved/reward_experiments/.','- Generalization data and plots: results/improved/generalization/.','- DRL tuning data and plots: results/improved/drl_experiments/.','- Final audit CSVs: results/final_audit/.','', '## Commands','','Install project dependencies with `pip install -r requirements.txt`. Run `pytest -q` for the normal test suite. The new experiments are reproduced with `python -m smart_dice_rl.gamma_sweep`, `python -m smart_dice_rl.gamma_sweep_all_boards`, `python -m smart_dice_rl.reward_experiments`, `python -m smart_dice_rl.run_generalization`, and `python -m smart_dice_rl.drl_tuning`. Generate analysis figures with `python -m smart_dice_rl.final_plots`.','','## Remaining limitations','','- DRL policies did not show reliable transfer to held-out 100-square layouts within 10,000–15,000 steps.','- The robust gamma sweep tests training-seed variability on three fixed original boards; it does not prove performance across a population of board layouts.','- New reward experiments were tabular-only and use 5,000 episodes; DQN/PPO/A2C reward variants were not separately trained.','- Potential-based shaping has the noted finite truncation caveat.','- Inference latency is CPU- and hardware-specific.','- The original random-dice extension was optional and was not substituted for the assignment’s controllable-dice core environment.']
out.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
print(f'Wrote {out}')

